From e63549cd6f12012c67c496338d5fc61e95fae559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luca abeni <luca.abeni@santannapisa.it>
Date: Tue, 7 Jan 2025 23:04:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] sched/deadline: Hierarchical scheduling with DL on top
 of RT

The runtime of RT tasks controlled by CGroups are enforced by the
SCHED_DEADLINE scheduling class, based on the runtime and period (the
deadline is set equal to the period) parameters.

sched_dl_entity may also represent a group of RT tasks, providing a rt_rq.

Fix zeroing runtime of rt cgroup
overflow checks did not allow to zero the runtime of a cgroup.
Add check to return value of dl_init_tg in free_rt_sched_group.

Check for the return value of dl_server_apply_params on initialization of the fair server

Fair server better checks
In dl_server_start, initialize the server if it really is a fair server,
regardless of its period value. inc_dl_task and dec_dl_task should increase/decrease
by one the value of active tasks if a fair_server starts/stops, while rt-cgroups
dl_servers are not accounted.

Co-authored-by: Yuri Andriaccio <y.andriaccio@studenti.unipi.it>
